    "verdict": "Quotient restriction makes a_K DEFINED but does NOT recover it: worst |quotient vs closed| = 1.070e+09 ppm. The LP reduces to y0* = min_i |contrib_i| (verified on all 6 atoms), so the dual carries no operator-selection content. Convention C missed by up to 1.6e17 ppm, so this is NOT a convention-D regression — D turned a wrong number into no number. Scope-(a): refutes the LP AS POSED (t = |contrib| against a sum-to-target constraint); does NOT exclude an operator-selection LP as the route to a_K.",
